the next generation of models to the use of AI in children's toys.","elementId":null,"dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":null}],"dateCreated":"Tue Sep 02 2025 18:03:51 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Tue May 05 2026 16:14:42 GMT+0000 (UTC)","shortBio":"Jared Perlo is a technology reporter focused on AI for NBC News Digital.","liveBlogShortBio":"","experience":[],"educationAndExpertise":[{"type":"markup","element":"div","html":"\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eBefore joining NBC News, I was an AI policy researcher. I focused on robots, geopolitics and access to AI systems around the world. Prior to that, I worked on global health and development economics.","elementId":null,"dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":null}],"awards":[],"id":"ncpn1312649","email":"Jared.Perlo@nbcuni.com","jobTitle":[],"name":"Jared Perlo","primaryImage":{"altText":null,"height":1500,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/newscms/2026_19/3725325/260505-1x1-jared-perlo-headshot-vl-1211p.jpg"},"width":1500},"publisher":{"name":"nbcnews","subType":null,"type":"organization"},"socialMediaProfiles":{"email":null,"facebook":null,"instagram":null,"pinterest":null,"snapchat":null,"tiktok":null,"twitter":null,"whatsapp":null,"youtube":null,"mastodon":null,"threads":null,"signal":null},"subType":null,"type":"person","url":{"canonical":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/jared-perlo-ncpn1312649","primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/jared-perlo-ncpn1312649","short":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/jared-perlo-ncpn1312649","slug":"jared-perlo-ncpn1312649"},"worksFor":null,"content":{"pagination":{"offset":0,"page":1,"size":3,"totalItems":156,"totalPages":52},"items":[{"contentSharing":[{"publisher":"TODAY","unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"url":{"canonical":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","primary":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","short":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","slug":"two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086"}}],"id":"rcna597086","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:33:24 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Two AI researchers leave Anthropic and Google over safety concerns: ‘There are no adults in the room’"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"description":{"primary":"After Jacob Coxon roiled the AI industry with his viral departure from Anthropic, two more researchers are speaking out about their concerns over AI safety."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"The Anthropic PBC company logo on a shelf in London.","height":1666,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-anthropic-ch-1433-ff98e1.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null},{"contentSharing":[],"id":"rcna596767","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/anthropic-safety-researcher-resigned-warning-rapid-ai-development-gamb-rcna596767"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 00:57:13 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Anthropic safety researcher resigned with a warning about AI"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"description":{"primary":"Exclusive: In a message on Slack, Jacob Coxon told colleagues that without action, superintelligent AI has “a risk of causing human extinction.”"},"teaseImage":{"altText":"Image: Jacob Coxon wearing glasses and headphones.","height":1406,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-jacob-coxon-rs-7970e4.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null},{"contentSharing":[{"publisher":"TODAY","unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"url":{"canonical":"https://www.today.com/tech/tech-news/us-accuses-china-ai-developers-deepseek-alibaba-copying-american-ai-rcna596696","primary":"https://www.today.com/tech/tech-news/us-accuses-china-ai-developers-deepseek-alibaba-copying-american-ai-rcna596696","short":"https://www.today.com/tech/tech-news/us-accuses-china-ai-developers-deepseek-alibaba-copying-american-ai-rcna596696","slug":"us-accuses-china-ai-developers-deepseek-alibaba-copying-american-ai-rcna596696"}}],"id":"rcna596696","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/us-accuses-china-ai-developers-deepseek-alibaba-copying-american-ai-rcna596696"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Wed Sep 09 2026 08:42:21 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"U.S. agencies say top Chinese AI companies systematically copied American models"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"description":{"primary":"In its most detailed accusation yet, the U.S. government has named six Chinese AI companies that it says copied American companies for their AI secrets."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"Tiananmen Square and the Great Hall of the People in Beijing Ahead of NPC","height":1666,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-06/260604-china-rs-d9bdae.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null}]}}},{"type":"embeddedPerson","authorType":"contributor","featuredAuthor":{"isFeaturedAuthor":false},"person":{"bio":[{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Tom Llamas is anchor and managing editor of NBC Nightly News with Tom Llamas and anchor of Top Story with Tom Llamas, a daily streaming primetime newscast on NBC News NOW. In his role, Llamas leads breaking news and political coverage for NBC News and NBC News NOW.","elementId":null,"dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":null}],"dateCreated":"Fri Jun 25 2021 02:57:13 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Thu Jan 08 2026 18:08:43 GMT+0000 (UTC)","shortBio":"Tom Llamas is the anchor of \"Nightly News\" and \"Top Story\" on NBC News.","liveBlogShortBio":"","experience":[],"educationAndExpertise":[],"awards":[],"id":"ncpn1272326","email":null,"jobTitle":["NBC News’ Senior National Correspondent; Anchor, \"Top Story With Tom Llamas\" on NBC News NOW"],"name":"Tom Llamas","primaryImage":{"altText":null,"height":465,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/newscms/2025_39/3705787/250305-tom-llamas-cs-fa837a.jpg"},"width":696},"publisher":{"name":"nbcnews","subType":null,"type":"organization"},"socialMediaProfiles":{"email":null,"facebook":null,"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/llamasnbc/?hl=en","pinterest":null,"snapchat":null,"tiktok":null,"twitter":"@LlamasNBC","whatsapp":null,"youtube":null,"mastodon":null,"threads":null,"signal":null},"subType":null,"type":"person","url":{"canonical":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/tom-llamas-ncpn1272326","primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/tom-llamas-ncpn1272326","short":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/tom-llamas-ncpn1272326","slug":"tom-llamas-ncpn1272326"},"worksFor":null,"content":{"pagination":{"offset":0,"page":1,"size":3,"totalItems":54,"totalPages":18},"items":[{"contentSharing":[{"publisher":"TODAY","unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"url":{"canonical":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","primary":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","short":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","slug":"two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086"}}],"id":"rcna597086","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:33:24 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Two AI researchers leave Anthropic and Google over safety concerns: ‘There are no adults in the room’"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"description":{"primary":"After Jacob Coxon roiled the AI industry with his viral departure from Anthropic, two more researchers are speaking out about their concerns over AI safety."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"The Anthropic PBC company logo on a shelf in London.","height":1666,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-anthropic-ch-1433-ff98e1.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null},{"contentSharing":[],"id":"rcna596840","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/dementia-taking-toll-sept-11-responders-federal-health-program-doesnt-rcna596840"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:01:26 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Dementia is taking a toll on Sept. 11 responders. A federal health program doesn’t cover it."},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/cost-of-denial","text":"Cost of Denial","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/cost-of-denial"}},"description":{"primary":"Doctors and scientists are pushing to get dementia added to a list of conditions connected to Sept. 11."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"Stephen and Theresa Stolarik.","height":1666,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260908-cost-of-denial-dementia-9-11-ch-1259-cd8970.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null},{"contentSharing":[],"id":"rcna345260","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/chinas-race-dominate-humanoid-robotics-industry-rcna345260"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Fri May 15 2026 15:20:04 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Inside China’s race to dominate humanoid robotics industry"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"description":{"primary":"Beijing has put the robotics industry front and center of its national agenda as the tech race with Washington heats up in several key areas, including AI. "},"teaseImage":{"altText":"","height":1667,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-05/260515-robots-4-rs-695f37.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null}]}}},{"type":"embeddedPerson","authorType":"contributor","featuredAuthor":{"isFeaturedAuthor":false},"person":{"bio":[{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Christine Romans is the chief business correspondent at NBC News.","elementId":null,"dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":null}],"dateCreated":"Thu Nov 02 2023 13:40:04 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Tue May 12 2026 18:07:10 GMT+0000 (UTC)","shortBio":null,"liveBlogShortBio":"","experience":[],"educationAndExpertise":[],"awards":[],"id":"ncpn1307836","email":" christine.romans@nbcuni.com","jobTitle":[],"name":"Christine Romans","primaryImage":{"altText":null,"height":450,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/newscms/2024_10/3640959/christine_romans.jpg"},"width":450},"publisher":{"name":"nbcnews","subType":null,"type":"organization"},"socialMediaProfiles":{"email":null,"facebook":null,"instagram":null,"pinterest":null,"snapchat":null,"tiktok":null,"twitter":null,"whatsapp":null,"youtube":null,"mastodon":null,"threads":null,"signal":null},"subType":null,"type":"person","url":{"canonical":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/christine-romans-ncpn1307836","primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/christine-romans-ncpn1307836","short":"https://www.nbcnews.com/author/christine-romans-ncpn1307836","slug":"christine-romans-ncpn1307836"},"worksFor":null,"content":{"pagination":{"offset":0,"page":1,"size":3,"totalItems":74,"totalPages":25},"items":[{"contentSharing":[{"publisher":"TODAY","unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/trump-tariffs","text":"Trump tariffs","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-tariffs"}},"url":{"canonical":"https://www.today.com/business/economy/lutnick-trump-5000-check-taxpayer-funds-rcna597092","primary":"https://www.today.com/business/economy/lutnick-trump-5000-check-taxpayer-funds-rcna597092","short":"https://www.today.com/business/economy/lutnick-trump-5000-check-taxpayer-funds-rcna597092","slug":"lutnick-trump-5000-check-taxpayer-funds-rcna597092"}}],"id":"rcna597092","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/lutnick-trump-5000-check-taxpayer-funds-rcna597092"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Fri Sep 11 2026 16:31:41 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Lutnick says Trump’s $5,000 checks for Americans wouldn’t rely on taxpayer funds"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/trump-tariffs","text":"Trump tariffs","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-tariffs"}},"description":{"primary":"President Donald Trump’s promised $5,000 “dividend” for all U.S. adults would not be paid for with taxpayer dollars, Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick said."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick spoke to NBC News in a wide-ranging interview at the 9/11 Memorial \u0026 Museum in New York on Sept. 10, 2026.","height":1667,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260911-howard-lutnick-ew-1211p-af5174.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null},{"contentSharing":[{"publisher":"TODAY","unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/section/business/energy","text":"Energy","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/energy"}},"url":{"canonical":"https://www.today.com/business/energy/diesel-record-price-trump-inflation-rcna596843","primary":"https://www.today.com/business/energy/diesel-record-price-trump-inflation-rcna596843","short":"https://www.today.com/business/energy/diesel-record-price-trump-inflation-rcna596843","slug":"diesel-record-price-trump-inflation-rcna596843"}}],"id":"rcna596843","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/energy/diesel-record-price-trump-inflation-rcna596843"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Fri Sep 11 2026 09:31:49 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Diesel hits all-time high of $6 per gallon, and just about everything will cost more"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/section/business/energy","text":"Energy","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/energy"}},"description":{"primary":"“We are endangering one of the strongest economic pillars that we have in this country,” said fourth-generation Iowa farmer Mark Mueller."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"Drivers refuel trucks with diesel fuel at a Pilot gas station","height":1335,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260909-diesel-gas-station-vl-417p-bc7375.jpg"},"width":2000},"primaryImage":null},{"contentSharing":[{"publisher":"TODAY","unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"url":{"canonical":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","primary":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","short":"https://www.today.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086","slug":"two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086"}}],"id":"rcna597086","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/security/two-ai-researchers-leave-anthropic-google-safety-concerns-rcna597086"},"vertical":"news","datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:33:24 GMT+0000 (UTC)","headline":{"primary":"Two AI researchers leave Anthropic and Google over safety concerns: ‘There are no adults in the room’"},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":"nbcnews/collection/artificial-intelligence","text":"Artificial intelligence","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/artificial-intelligence"}},"description":{"primary":"After Jacob Coxon roiled the AI industry with his viral departure from Anthropic, two more researchers are speaking out about their concerns over AI safety."},"teaseImage":{"altText":"The Anthropic PBC company logo on a shelf in London.","height":1666,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-anthropic-ch-1433-ff98e1.jpg"},"width":2500},"primaryImage":null}]}}}],"adsEnabled":true,"ecommerceEnabled":false,"sponsoredBy":null,"hidden":false,"searchable":true,"nativeAd":false,"breakingNews":false,"breakingTagDisabled":true,"body":[{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Citing fears that AI systems may soon spiral out of human control and potentially kill all humans, two more researchers from Anthropic and Google DeepMind who recently left their coveted positions are sounding the alarm about risks from advanced AI systems. ","elementId":"7bdb9d","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Joe Benton, who used to lead a safety research team at Anthropic, and Josh Engels, who used to work on AI safety research at Google, told NBC News in their first interviews since they left that they see an urgent need to boost transparency about incidents at the cutting edge of AI given the rapid pace of AI development.","elementId":"9f2f56","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Advances in AI research “could speed up the pace of progress from merely blistering at the minute to uncontrollable” rates of development, Benton said in an interview with Tom Llamas. ","elementId":"c35f84","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“There are no adults in the room,” Engels added. “People are trying their best, but there is no one coming to save us.”","elementId":"f94378","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Benton and Engels spoke with NBC News in the wake of a viral social media post from former Anthropic researcher Jacob Coxon, who left Anthropic on Tuesday. In \u003ca href=\"https://x.com/hilbertspaess/status/2097476196791709843\" target=\"_blank\"\u003ehis post on X\u003c/a\u003e announcing his departure, Coxon highlighted his extreme concern about the pace of AI development and the risks he believes it poses to the future of humanity. The post has been viewed more than 155 million times, spurring calls from legislators to hold special sessions of Congress to take action and sparking a wave of AI employees to speak out in support of his concerns. ","elementId":"31f7c5","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Benton and Engels both pointed to the \u003ca href=\"https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-model-evaluation-security-incident/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003erecent cyberattack against AI startup Hugging Face\u003c/a\u003e, carried out in July by autonomous AI systems powered by an unreleased OpenAI model, as part of the reason for shifting their work now. ","elementId":"609535","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"presentation":{"alignment":"left","size":"small","style":"default","byline":null,"hideRecommendations":false,"hideProductRecommendations":false},"type":"embeddedImage","image":{"id":"rcim564526","headline":{"primary":null,"tease":null,"seo":null,"social":null},"caption":" Josh Engels, who used to work on AI safety research at Google.","altText":"","url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-FORMER-AI-EMPLOYEES-ww-1521-1-def0df.jpg"},"imageUrl":{"aims":"https://media1.s-nbcnews.com/i/rockcms/2026-09/564526/260910-FORMER-AI-EMPLOYEES-ww-1521-1-def0df_7aebb191c3882f7ca771e3e6507638c9815b87a0.jpg","cloudinary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-FORMER-AI-EMPLOYEES-ww-1521-1-def0df.jpg","telemundo":null},"encodingFormat":"image/jpeg","height":1600,"width":1594,"authors":[{"name":""}],"source":{"name":"via Josh Engels","copyright":null},"graphicContent":false,"imageContentType":[]},"elementId":"577ad3"},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“If you look at some of the recent incidents, these were not cases where humans told the models to do something bad,” Engels said. Instead, OpenAI’s AI systems autonomously decided to hack into Hugging Face’s systems, create a sort of illicit message board to exchange information and even expose some of OpenAI’s own computing infrastructure to the open internet.","elementId":"bdba8a","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“The models decided that the best way to to accomplish their task was to commit really egregious actions, to commit crimes,” Engels said in an interview with Christine Romans.","elementId":"cfd5bd","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"OpenAI said that it has since strengthened its safeguards and that newer public models, including its most recent Astra system, more reliably follow human instructions.","elementId":"634b73","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"An Anthropic spokesperson said in a statement Wednesday: “We have always been transparent that AI will bring both enormous benefits and unprecedented risks. To address these risks, we continue to build models with some of the strongest safeguards in the industry.”","elementId":"515994","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Benton managed a group at Anthropic dedicated to creating ways for humans and weaker AI systems to supervise more capable AI systems. He said that he is particularly worried that the public does not have significant insight into how AI systems have already exceeded the bounds of human instructions and that \u003ca href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/chatgpt-openai-ai-agent-rogue-anthropic-clause-security-cyber-rcna592417\" target=\"_blank\"\u003ethe lack of transparency\u003c/a\u003e could only get worse as systems become more capable. ","elementId":"27402b","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"presentation":{"alignment":"left","size":"small","style":"default","byline":null,"hideRecommendations":false,"hideProductRecommendations":false},"type":"embeddedImage","image":{"id":"rcim564527","headline":{"primary":null,"tease":null,"seo":null,"social":null},"caption":"Joe Benton, who used to lead a safety research team at Anthropic.","altText":"","url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-FORMER-AI-EMPLOYEES-ww-1521-2-961660.jpg"},"imageUrl":{"aims":"https://media1.s-nbcnews.com/i/rockcms/2026-09/564527/260910-FORMER-AI-EMPLOYEES-ww-1521-2-961660_88373c1ae98014529f4ce460a671e962576367e5.jpg","cloudinary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/rockcms/2026-09/260910-FORMER-AI-EMPLOYEES-ww-1521-2-961660.jpg","telemundo":null},"encodingFormat":"image/jpeg","height":1158,"width":926,"authors":[{"name":""}],"source":{"name":"via Joe Benton","copyright":null},"graphicContent":false,"imageContentType":[]},"elementId":"58a0b1"},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“At the minute, basically all of the transparency about these risks that is coming from the companies is entirely voluntary,” Benton told NBC News. ","elementId":"3bc839","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"In a \u003ca href=\"https://openai.com/index/ai-policy-window/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eblog post released Wednesday\u003c/a\u003e, OpenAI’s head of global affairs, Chris Lehane, agreed that the status quo is insufficient. “Today, frontier laboratories largely set their own rules for managing frontier risks,” Lehane wrote. “Democratically accountable standards, independent verification, and meaningful transparency would replace that fragmented system of private governance.”","elementId":"1a2c21","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"No federal law mandates that the largest AI companies, like OpenAI and Anthropic, share reports when agents or AI systems act beyond humans’ control.","elementId":"216450","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"embeddedVideo","disablePlaylistAutoplay":false,"presentation":{"alignment":"left","size":"medium","style":"default","byline":null,"hideRecommendations":false,"hideProductRecommendations":false},"video":{"id":"mmvo269663301684","contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]},"associatedVideoPlaylist":{"id":"mmlsnnd_18424776-nnd","headline":{"primary":"Nightly News"},"videos":[{"type":"v