 on edge","social":"Mid-air scares leave passengers on edge"},"description":{"primary":"Multiple mid-air scares left passengers on edge this week, including one that led to passengers being zip-tied and handcuffed after they got into a fight on board. NBC News’ Aaron Gilchrist reports."},"publisher":{"name":"nbcnews"},"source":{"name":"Nightly News","roles":[]},"taxonomy":{"additionalTerms":[{"dateCreated":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:36:46 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:36:46 GMT+0000 (UTC)","description":{"primary":null},"id":"nctx19","isCurated":true,"name":"Nightly News","path":"nbcnews/show/nightly-news","pageRoute":"/nightly-news","slug":"nightly-news","type":"taxonomy","taxonomyType":"show","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/nightly-news"}}],"primaryVertical":{"name":"News"},"primarySection":null,"primaryTopic":null},"hasCaptions":true,"closedCaptioning":{"smptett":null,"srt":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/captions/2026/09/1789339455576_wnn_ag_airplanescares_260913.srt","webvtt":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/captions/2026/09/1789339455576_wnn_ag_airplanescares_260913.vtt"},"videoAssets":[{"assetType":"EMP","format":"M3U","publicUrl":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/wnn_ag_airplanescares_260913/1/abs/index.m3u8","height":1080,"width":1920,"assetDuration":86.62,"bitrate":4195000},{"assetType":"akamaiMp4","format":"MPEG4","publicUrl":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/video/2026/09/1789339455576_wnn_ag_airplanescares_260913_6.mp4","height":1080,"width":1920,"assetDuration":86.62,"bitrate":4195438}]}]},"taxonomy":{"additionalTerms":[{"dateCreated":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:36:46 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:36:46 GMT+0000 (UTC)","description":{"primary":null},"id":"nctx19","isCurated":true,"name":"Nightly News","path":"nbcnews/show/nightly-news","pageRoute":"/nightly-news","slug":"nightly-news","type":"taxonomy","taxonomyType":"show","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/nightly-news"}},{"dateCreated":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:38:03 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:38:03 GMT+0000 (UTC)","description":{"primary":null},"id":"nctx75","isCurated":true,"name":"Tech","path":"nbcnews/section/tech","pageRoute":"/tech-media","slug":"tech","type":"taxonomy","taxonomyType":"section","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech-media"}},{"dateCreated":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:10:17 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Thu Sep 16 2021 03:10:17 GMT+0000 (UTC)","description":{"primary":null},"id":"nctx29","isCurated":true,"name":"Consumer","path":"nbcnews/section/business/consumer","pageRoute":"/business/consumer","slug":"consumer","type":"taxonomy","taxonomyType":"topic","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/consumer"}}],"primaryVertical":{"name":"News","taxonomyType":"vertical"},"primarySection":null,"primaryTopic":null},"unibrow":{"logo":null,"taxonomyPath":null,"text":"Nightly News","url":{"primary":null}},"duration":"PT2M2S","dateCreated":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:43:12 GMT+0000 (UTC)","datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:43:13 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:49:39 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateBroadcast":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:43:16 GMT+0000 (UTC)","date":{"publishedAt":"2026-09-10T22:43:13.000Z","createdAt":"2026-09-10T22:43:12.000Z","modifiedAt":"2026-09-10T22:49:39.000Z"},"liveVideoStatus":"NONE","nativeAd":false,"mpxMetadata":{"id":"269663301684","guid":"nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026","externalAdvertiserId":"nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026","accountId":"2704722219","accountName":"nbcnewsdigital"},"source":{"name":"Nightly News"},"publisher":{"name":"nbcnews"},"partOfEpisode":null,"partOfSeason":null,"videoType":"broadcast","sentiment":"neutral","headline":{"primary":"Growing chorus of A.I. insiders warns of possible extinction of humans","tease":"Growing chorus of A.I. insiders warns of possible extinction of humans","seo":"Growing chorus of A.I. insiders warns of possible extinction of humans","social":"Growing chorus of A.I. insiders warns of possible extinction of humans"},"description":{"primary":"Former employees from some of the top A.I. companies say the potential of future models is nothing short of the killing of all humans. NBC News’ Christine Romans reports.","seo":"Former employees from some of the top A.I. companies say the potential of future models is nothing short of the killing of all humans. NBC News’ Christine Romans reports."},"playable":true,"url":{"canonical":"https://www.nbcnews.com/nightly-news/video/growing-chorus-of-a-i-insiders-warns-of-possible-extinction-of-humans-269663301684","primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/nightly-news/video/growing-chorus-of-a-i-insiders-warns-of-possible-extinction-of-humans-269663301684","short":"https://www.nbcnews.com/nightly-news/video/growing-chorus-of-a-i-insiders-warns-of-possible-extinction-of-humans-269663301684","slug":"growing-chorus-of-a-i-insiders-warns-of-possible-extinction-of-humans-269663301684"},"hasCaptions":true,"closedCaptioning":{"smptett":null,"srt":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/captions/2026/09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026.srt","webvtt":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/captions/2026/09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026.vtt"},"videoAssets":[{"assetType":"EMP","format":"M3U","publicUrl":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026/1/abs/index.m3u8","height":1080,"width":1920,"assetDuration":122.089,"bitrate":4148000},{"assetType":"akamaiMp4","format":"MPEG4","publicUrl":"https://prodamdnewsencoding.akamaized.net/NBC_News_Digital/nbcnews/video/2026/09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_6.mp4","height":1080,"width":1920,"assetDuration":122.089,"bitrate":4148434}],"primaryImage":{"id":"vidimg3638331209","headline":{"primary":null},"altText":null,"caption":null,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/mpx/2704722219/2026_09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_S3_1920x1080-5f6ozx.jpg"},"imageUrl":{"aims":"https://media14.s-nbcnews.com/i/mpx/2704722219/2026_09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_S3_1920x1080-5f6ozx.jpg","cloudinary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/mpx/2704722219/2026_09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_S3_1920x1080-5f6ozx.jpg","telemundo":null},"source":null,"authors":[],"height":null,"width":null,"graphicContent":false},"teaseImage":{"id":"vidimg3638331209","headline":{"primary":null},"altText":null,"caption":null,"url":{"primary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/mpx/2704722219/2026_09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_S3_1920x1080-5f6ozx.jpg"},"imageUrl":{"aims":"https://media14.s-nbcnews.com/i/mpx/2704722219/2026_09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_S3_1920x1080-5f6ozx.jpg","cloudinary":"https://media-cldnry.s-nbcnews.com/image/upload/mpx/2704722219/2026_09/1789080188298_nn_cro_ai_insiders_warning_26091026_S3_1920x1080-5f6ozx.jpg","telemundo":null},"source":null,"authors":[],"height":null,"width":null,"graphicContent":false},"documentTracing":{"currentMessageId":{"id":"365f59fb-d668-4019-921b-3f845e08d55b","updatedDate":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:49:48 GMT+0000 (UTC)"}},"relatedUrl":null,"relatedContentLink":{"text":null,"url":null}},"elementId":"b8394c"},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Benton and Engels are joining METR, one of the world’s leading AI safety nonprofit research centers, to work on investigations into incidents or episodes in which AI strays from human directions or intentions. METR aims to create scientific ways to evaluate how AI systems could cause catastrophic risks and empower researchers and the public to sway their development. ","elementId":"abf681","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“I left because I think I can have more positive influence on the development of this technology by helping to foster public transparency from outside these companies and to shed light on the risks,” Benton said. ","elementId":"07d109","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"The researchers joined growing numbers of AI safety researchers raising awareness about today’s AI systems following Coxon’s post Tuesday. Marcus Williams, an OpenAI employee who works on monitoring the activity of AI agents, wrote \u003ca href=\"https://x.com/Marcus_J_W/status/2098078076299366684\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eThursday afternoon on X\u003c/a\u003e, “Unless there is AI regulation or a coordinated slowdown between labs, human extinction in the next few years seems very likely.”","elementId":"d40955","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Geoffrey Irving, who was the chief scientist at the United Kingdom’s AI Security Institute and served stints at Google and OpenAI, seemed to agree Wednesday on X. “I think we have a ~50% chance of all dying as a result of superintelligence, mostly due to actions in the next few to 10 years.”","elementId":"5395ca","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"AI researchers have referenced the possibility that AI systems could potentially begin to improve themselves without human input, creating the potential for AI systems to either purposely or incidentally kill humans. ","elementId":"6ca6c1","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Benton said he was most worried that the pace of technological improvement could lead to this sort of digital or artificial superintelligence, in which AI systems are more capable than humans across most tasks. “All of these companies — and this is something I witnessed firsthand at Anthropic — are pretty directly trying to race towards automating the process of AI R\u0026D itself,” he said. ","elementId":"55eb2e","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Benton suggested that there’s a chance AI systems could come to exist as a sort of separate species before long. “We’re probably going to go from a world where we have very capable systems now to a world where potentially we are co-inhabiting a world with AI agents that are much, much smarter than humans at some point in the next few years,” he said.","elementId":"23a830","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Engels said many people outside the AI industry might not fully appreciate just how intelligent today’s AI systems already are — and how capable they might soon become. “We’re building these systems that are generally intelligent,” he said. “They can generally do what people can do, and soon they might be able to generally do what people can do, but better.”","elementId":"a926ae","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"Both researchers said they were excited to shift their attention to more public efforts to highlight the latest AI progress, so people can make more informed decisions.","elementId":"10a926","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“There are many reasons people are excited and racing forward, Engels said, citing huge potential upsides and benefits from AI. But he added that “we should progress as society aware of the risks and okay with where they’re at.”","elementId":"d24fe5","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}},{"type":"markup","element":"p","html":"“I am worried that stuff might end up progressing too fast for us to get our act together in time,” Benton said, “unless we worry about it now.”","elementId":"5a8985","dataAttributes":[],"contentRules":{"contentClassifications":["UNRESTRICTED"]}}],"datePublished":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:33:24 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateModified":"Mon Sep 14 2026 00:37:32 GMT+0000 (UTC)","dateCreated":"Thu Sep 10 2026 22:33:24 GMT+0000 (UTC)","source":null,"presentation":{"alignment":"left","size":"medium","style":"default","byline":"EXPANDED","hideRecommendations":false,"hideProductRecommendations":false},"publisher":{"name":"nbcnews"},"subnav":null,"eventDateTime":{"endsAt":null}}],"error":null,"isNativeAd":false,"presentation":{"alignment":"left","size":"medium","style":"default","byline":"EXPANDED","hideRecommendations":false,"hideProductRecommendations":false},"fetchingRelated":false,"relatedArticles":null,"isLoadingMostPopularStories":false,"mostPopularStoryList":{"callout":null,"content":{"pagination":{"totalItems":10},"items":[{"headline":{"tease":"Trump says AI doesn’t need guardrails, only a ‘high IQ’ president"},"id":"rcna597700","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/trump-administration/trump-rejects-ai-guardrails-rcna597700"}},{"headline":{"tease":"DHS watchdog finds immigrants held at ‘Alligator Alcatraz’ in outdoor cages the size of phone booths "},"id":"rcna593917","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/dhs-watchdog-immigrants-held-outdoor-cages-size-phone-booths-alligator-rcna593917"}},{"headline":{"tease":"Female athletes hit back at Sydney Sweeney’s sexualized ‘just sports’ ad"},"id":"rcna597489","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/sports/sports/female-athletes-hit-back-sydney-sweeneys-sexualized-just-sports-ad-rcna597489"}},{"headline":{"tease":"Man arrested after manhunt in deadly Louisiana stabbing spree"},"id":"rcna597545","url":{"primary":"https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/man-apprehended-manhun